of {nu}, it does not contrast with it. {pu'u}, {za'i}, {zu'o} and
{mu'e} are all {nu}, so by using {nu} you don't exclude the
{pu'u} interpretation. You can describe it as a process if you
are considering all the steps that constitute the flow from its
origin to its destination, you can describe it as an activity
if you see it as a continuous action, a state if you contrast
it with the non-flowing state as two binary options, and an
achievment if all you care about is its result, either it flowed
or it didn't flow.

